     "title": "Introducing Claude Fable 5.2 and Claude Mythos 5.2",
     "kind": "primary"
    }
   ],
   "headline": "Claude Fable 5.2 becomes the new top tier, with Mythos 5.2 for vetted security and life-science teams",
   "summary": "Anthropic released Claude Fable 5.2 (API id claude-fable-5-2) on all major clouds at $8 per million input tokens and $40 per million output tokens, or $16 and $80 in fast mode. Mythos 5.2 is the same underlying model with lighter cyber and biology restrictions, available only through Anthropic's verification programs. Anthropic still recommends starting most work on its current Opus model and moving up to Fable or down to Sonnet or Haiku as needed.",
   "curriculum_note": "Teach model tiering as a cost decision: run the same agent task on two tiers and have students justify the escalation with the price difference.",
   "details": [
    "Anthropic reports SWE v2 at 69.9% for Fable 5.2 against 62.3% for its current Opus model. These are the vendor's own numbers.",
    "The post describes Fable 5.2 building a prototype operating system over eight days with more than 1,000 subagents.",
    "Preserved thinking now applies to every API account, so integrations that handle thinking blocks should be checked."
   ],
