   "headline": "EU watermarking grace period ends Dec 2, 2026",
   "summary": "Under the AI Act amendments in Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, generative AI systems placed on the market before Aug 2, 2026 must meet the watermarking obligation by Dec 2, 2026. Newer systems have had to comply since Aug 2, and the other transparency duties in Article 50 also apply from that date. The Commission's voluntary Code of Practice on marking and labelling AI-generated content is the practical guide.",
   "curriculum_note": "Any demo app a cohort ships to EU users should mark generated content, label deepfakes, and tell users when they are talking to a chatbot.",
   "details": [
    "The amending regulation entered into force July 27, 2026. It moved Annex III high-risk duties to Dec 2, 2027 and Annex I duties to Aug 2, 2028.",
    "The AI literacy duty was softened: providers and deployers must take measures to support a sufficient level of AI literacy among staff."
